<% content_for :title, "House Affordability Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  House Affordability calculator page (spec issue #259, DESIGN.md BLEND) — the mortgage
  math run IN REVERSE: from income, recurring debts, down payment, rate/term and the
  lender's debt-to-income (DTI) ratios it derives the MAXIMUM monthly housing payment, then
  inverts amortization to the maximum loan amount and the maximum home price (the hero
  answer). The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works
  WITHOUT JS — the server validates and re-renders the result fragment. Stimulus is pure
  polish (the result's housing-budget donut).

  NO mode picker (spec Notes): one single-pass computation — the DTI ratios are ordinary
  numeric inputs, not a mode the inputs depend on. So a plain single-mode form (like
  Mortgage), DESIGN.md §4.

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to
  one column on mobile. The ten inputs are grouped into three labelled sub-sections (income
  & debt, the loan, the DTI limits + ownership costs) so the long form reads as related sets,
  not one undifferentiated stack. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card → mt-7/mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">House Affordability Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    How much house can you afford? Enter your
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">income</span>, recurring
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">debts</span>, your
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">down payment</span> and the loan terms, and we run the
    mortgage math in reverse — your lender's debt-to-income limits set the most you can spend on
    housing, and we work back to the maximum
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">home price</span>. Every figure is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/house_affordability", scope: :inputs, method: :post do |f| %>

      <%# ── Income & debt ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
          The income that the DTI ratios cap, and the recurring monthly debts the back-end
          ratio nets out. Stacked tier (space-y-5); each field carries its $ affix on the
          Affix tier (gap-2 — DESIGN.md §3). %>
      <fieldset class="space-y-5">
        <legend class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Income &amp; debt</legend>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :annual_income, "Annual income", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_annual_income" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :annual_income, id: "inputs_annual_income", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :monthly_debts, "Monthly debts", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_monthly_debts" %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">Recurring obligations — car, student loans, credit cards.</p>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :monthly_debts, id: "inputs_monthly_debts", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# ── The loan ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
          The down payment added back to the loan to reach the price, and the rate/term that
          invert amortization to the affordable principal. %>
      <fieldset class="mt-7 space-y-5">
        <legend class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">The loan</legend>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :down_payment, "Down payment", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_down_payment" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :down_payment, id: "inputs_down_payment", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :annual_rate, "Annual interest rate", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_annual_rate" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :annual_rate, id: "inputs_annual_rate", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :loan_term_years, "Loan term", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_loan_term_years" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :loan_term_years, id: "inputs_loan_term_years", step: "1", inputmode: "numeric",
                  min: "1", placeholder: "30", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="w-12 text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">years</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# ── DTI limits & ownership costs ────────────────────────────────────
          The two debt-to-income ratios (the front-end caps housing alone, the back-end caps
          housing + debts; the binding/smaller one wins) and the fixed monthly ownership costs
          that come out of the housing budget before P&I. A conventional 28 / 36 pair is the
          common default — placeholdered, not auto-filled (the values are entered, per spec). %>
      <fieldset class="mt-7 space-y-5">
        <legend class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">DTI limits &amp; ownership costs</legend>

        <%# The two DTI ratios side by side — a wrapping control group, so the row-gap is one
            step larger than the column-gap (DESIGN.md §3 "Grouped, wrapping"). %>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-4">
          <div class="min-w-[8rem] flex-1">
            <%= f.label :front_dti, "Front-end DTI", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_front_dti" %>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
              <%= f.number_field :front_dti, id: "inputs_front_dti", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                    min: "0", max: "100", placeholder: "28", class: "field-input" %>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-[8rem] flex-1">
            <%= f.label :back_dti, "Back-end DTI", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_back_dti" %>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
              <%= f.number_field :back_dti, id: "inputs_back_dti", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                    min: "0", max: "100", placeholder: "36", class: "field-input" %>
              <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :monthly_property_tax, "Monthly property tax", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_monthly_property_tax" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :monthly_property_tax, id: "inputs_monthly_property_tax", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :monthly_home_insurance, "Monthly home insurance", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_monthly_home_insurance" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :monthly_home_insurance, id: "inputs_monthly_home_insurance", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <%= f.label :monthly_hoa, "Monthly HOA fee", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_monthly_hoa" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :monthly_hoa, id: "inputs_monthly_hoa", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
